{%- comment -%}
  Outputs "hidden" when a page should be kept out of search results.

  Shopify's search covers every published page, which drops app-generated
  pages (the Avada SEO HTML sitemaps) into the results next to the rings. The
  real fix is deleting those pages in the admin; this keeps them off the
  storefront in the meantime, and keeps any other page a merchant does not
  want found out of the results without unpublishing it.

  Matched on the title, case-insensitively, against the terms in
  Theme settings > Search behaviour > "Hide pages whose title contains".

  Usage:
    {%- capture hide_page -%}
      {%- render 'search-page-hidden', page_title: item.title -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if hide_page contains 'hidden' -%}...{%- endif -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign hidden_terms = settings.search_hidden_page_titles | downcase | split: '|'
  assign haystack = page_title | downcase

  for term in hidden_terms
    assign needle = term | strip
    if needle != blank and haystack contains needle
      echo 'hidden'
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
